    "created_at": "2024-03-14T17:35:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-03-14T17:43:28Z",
    "body": "Label is an interactive element for pointers/touch that focuses the associated interactive element. I'd only be in favor of this **IF** browser vendors confirm they can support this feature.\r\n\r\nAside from that, `<legend>` works just fine. Especially considering my above comment, what's the expected behavior of mouse click on a `<label>` in a `<fieldset>`? First interactive? First empty?\r\n\r\nLastly, I think `contenteditable` is really hard to label. Often, it's whatever the user puts in there. And how often do you see a label for this? Personally, never. A tooltip (cringe)/description explaining how to use it, visual affordances that it's editable are all helpful but not getting a lift from `<label>` unless this is just enabling authors to replace actual proper form elements with `<label>` + `contenteditable` in which case I'm against. ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
